cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this guide, its docs, or repo_kit's templates, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
title: research-software-field-guide
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  A practical guide to writing trustworthy research software, aimed at scientists who
  didn't train as software developers. Walks from first terminal use through version
  control, testing, code review, running rigorous experiments, and citable releases,
  and includes a portable standard (repo_kit/) for bringing any existing research
  repository up to the same practices.
authors:
  - family-names: Dennis
    given-names: Allison
    affiliation: Northeastern University
    email: a.dennis@northeastern.edu
repository-code: "https://github.com/AllisonMDennis/research-software-field-guide"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - research software
  - reproducibility
  - open science
  - scientific computing
  - software engineering education
